{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Great</b> — Because he mentioned \"and I will praise Your name,\" he stated that HaShem is greater than what is praised of Him, therefore: \"and highly praised,\" more than what they praise Him. And because he said that He is great, he noted that His greatness has no limit, for every king besides Him—his greatness has a beginning and an end, but His greatness is not so."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:46.200545922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}